A. Wyatt wrote:
>
> After emptying the wine cellar of loot and hauling every single item
> of interest back to the minetown altar, I set to the tedious task of
> identifying everything.

I notice there are unidentified boots in your box.  Is it poosible they
are water walking?  Try to identify them fully.  Try jumping with and
without them,  Wear them long enough to be sure they are not fumble.
Look for ways to tell if they improve kicking damage.  Your hope is
they are water walking because of:

> The RNG has denied me holy water or blessed

You have plenty of potions.  You have a known altar.  If you have a
way to #dip those potions into water you will have a ready supply
of holy water.

> I cleared the next several dungeon levels methodically, keeping my
> stash by the altar on level 4 (and later hauling the entire darn chest
> down to level 7), and encountered a big room for the first time in my
> career as a nethacker.  The room was a bit anticlimactic, as it only
> contained monsters that I was confident I could melee down with a
> minimum of fuss.  After considering my position for a while, I charged
> right in and had no real trouble, however my trusty dog died to the
> poisoned blade of an A.  I should have realized that a domestic animal
> can't be expected to continue to be effective in combat indefinitely.

Pets use the naked meanness of monsters so they don't take
weapons into effect.  That A is carrying rustproof items so it might
be worth getting him to leave you them in his will.  Having a spare
rustproof long sword and a rustproof shield doesn't suck.

> pass up).  I've obtained a decent stock of stuff, and my AC is -17
> (it'll be -20 if I can manage to foo-proof some of these armor
> pieces). 

Some pieces are already naturally immune.  Others are not worth
rustproofing IMO.  Be selective.

> I carry 3 unicorn horns and 4 lizard corpses,

In both cases 1 in the inventory the rest in a nearby stash.  Do you
know much about horns and potions?

> My luck is certainly bad, because I've foolishly kept
> my luckstone out since cheating in Sokoban.

Into the bag with it immediately until you have done some sacrifesting
to correct alignment and luck.  Also note that blessing it will cause
negative luck to drift towards zero.

> I fear my god and
> alignment are unhappy as well; ever since killing that shopkeeper I've
> been afraid to pray, and I've also gotten in the habit of killing and
> eating peaceful Tengu

Sacrifice only until you are certain you can pray.

> in hopes of no longer having to wear my =oTC.
> (5 corpses and still no intrinsic).

If you haven't tried 50+ you haven't tried enough.  In Nethack the
number of digits tends to be higher than you expected.

>  a - the blessed rustproof +3 Excalibur (weapon in hand)

You have access to a rustproof spare at least +0.

>  X - 3 uncursed daggers

Use Q to put them in your quiver.  Always have quivered missile
weapons no matter your skill level at throwing.

>  s - an uncursed ring called shiny ring of see invisible (on left
> hand)

There's something about stalkers ...

>  d - an uncursed bag of tricks

Sacrifest fodder.  Excellent.

>  F - an uncursed lock pick

I thought you had killed a shopkeeper?  This should be a key.

>  a - an uncursed +0 elven cloak

Competition for the orcish cloak.  But at +5 you may never enchant
the orcish cloak but it's too nice to not use it.  You get MC#3 from
your mithril for the moment.

>  c - an uncursed tin

On the chance it's spinach, eat it first as soon as you are hungry.

>  Potions
>  o - a cursed potion of extra healing
>  p - a blessed potion of object detection
>  q - 3 uncursed potions called potion of booze
>  a - a blessed potion of healing
>  b - 2 uncursed potions of healing
>  c - an uncursed potion of full healing
>  d - 3 uncursed potions of extra healing

Some need to be dipped to water, others kept for alchemy.

>  j - an uncursed wand of polymorph

Interesting.  And you have tons of items in the mines.  This may
supply you with interesting items.

>  j - an uncursed stone called luck stone

Into bag now until your luck is healed, blessed as soon as you have a
ready supply of holy water.

> Contents of the large box named stash (by the > on Dlvl 7):
>  l - an uncursed +0 pair of jungle boots

Make certain you know what this is.   If it is water walking you can
use it to have a ready supply of holy water.

>  Comestibles
>  n - a cursed tin

Interesting thing about prayer once your luck is high - Sometimes
cursed items in your inventory are uncursed.  So when you are sure
you can pray, have as many cursed items in your open inventory as
you can manage.

>  o - 4 uncursed lumps of royal jelly

Strength is good.  Eat these as soon as you are hungry.

>  q - 4 uncursed K-rations
>  a - 7 uncursed C-rations

Long term stash building towards end game.

>  f - 2 cursed scrolls of create monster

Sacrifest fodder.

>  Potions
>  i - a blessed potion called murky fruit juice
>  j - an uncursed potion called murky fruit juice
>  k - an uncursed clear potion
>  l - an uncursed potion called potion of confusion
>  m - a cursed potion called potion of booze
>  n - a blessed potion called potion of confusion
>  o - an uncursed potion of hallucination
>  p - a cursed potion called potion of sickness
>  q - a cursed potion of gain energy
>  r - 3 uncursed potions called potion of see invisible
>  s - an uncursed potion of monster detection
>  t - an uncursed potion of sleeping
>  u - 2 uncursed potions called potion of gain ability
>  a - an uncursed potion of gain energy
>  b - 2 potions of object detection
>  c - 4 uncursed potions of paralysis
>  d - 7 uncursed potions of object detection
>  e - a potion called murky fruit juice
>  f - a cursed potion of monster detection

Dip into water, keep for other reasons, keep for alchemy, learn which.

>  a - an uncursed blindfold

I think this is better than a towel.

>  Gems
>  d - 3 uncursed red gems

A long list.  No idea if you want to partially identify them.  It is
easy to learn hard versus soft and all hard are valuable.  Once
fast it is tedious to learn the glass types among the soft ones.
Once you know that keep or sell the valuable ones and use the
glass ones either for polypile fodder or as missiles.  Thrown
glass gems hit as hard as thrown rocks but they weight 1/10th
as much.


